#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188034 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188327 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c80ef8f-1073-5e41-bec3-860209a731bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional Mass Function"}] :question/id #uuid "6cdc2b0e-a968-5d95-8fb6-5d469a5920b9" :question/math-academy-id "e-10302" :question/problem "| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, 3)$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\textrm{Var}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X=3\\big\\end{bmatrix}$ given that the conditional probability mass function $f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, 3)$ is shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is $\\mu_{Y \\mid 3} = \\dfrac{8}{3}$." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = x\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}(Y - μ_{Y \\mid x})^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{Y\\begin{vmatrix}x}^{2} \\\\ = [∑_(y)y^{2}f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid x)] - μ_{Y\\end{vmatrix}x}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = 3\\end{bmatrix} &= [∑_(y)y^{2}f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid 3)] - μ_{Y \\mid 3}^{2} \\\\\n&= [(1)^{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} + (2)^{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} + (4)^{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}] - (\\frac{8}{3})^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{2}{3} + 8 - \\frac{64}{9} \\\\\n&= \\frac{17}{9}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188035 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188328 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92a52324-627c-5796-bc4f-ddeb5380f129" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Using Column Totals"}] :question/id #uuid "49a039ae-dbe1-5faa-a9a7-014bd9549c03" :question/math-academy-id "e-10306" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{16}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{16}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\textrm{Var}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}X \\, & \\, Y=2\\big\\end{bmatrix}$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is $\\mu_{X \\mid 2}=\\dfrac{10}{9}$." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}X & Y = y\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}(X - μ_{X \\mid y})^{2} & Y = y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\\begin{bmatrix}X^{2} & Y = y\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{X\\begin{vmatrix}y}^{2} \\\\ = [∑_(x)x^{2}f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid y)] - μ_{X\\end{vmatrix}y}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find $f_{X \\mid Y}(x \\, \\mid \\, y)$, let's first find the marginal distribution of $Y$, corresponding to the column totals:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{16}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{16}$ |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $\\dfrac{9}{16}$ | $\\dfrac{7}{16}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\nf_{X \\mid Y}(x \\, \\mid \\, y) = \\dfrac{f(x,y)}{f_Y(y)}\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y{:}$\n\n| $f_{X\\mid Y}(x\\, \\mid \\,y)$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{8}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{4}{7}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{7}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}X & Y = 2\\end{bmatrix} &= [∑_(x)x^{2}f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid 2)] - μ_{X \\mid 2}^{2} \\\\\n&= [1^{2} \\cdot \\frac{8}{9} + 2^{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{9}] - (\\frac{10}{9})^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{8}{9} + \\frac{4}{9} - \\frac{100}{81} \\\\\n&= \\frac{8}{81}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188046 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abfaf356-6b74-5dfd-8070-e3a60dc372c5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Using Row Totals"}] :question/id #uuid "3764cb54-7fd2-584a-9dc7-eda88368b032" :question/math-academy-id "e-10352" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{3}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\textrm{Var}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X=1\\big\\end{bmatrix}$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is $\\mu_{Y \\mid 1} = \\dfrac{9}{4}$." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = x\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}(Y - μ_{Y \\mid x})^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{Y\\begin{vmatrix}x}^{2} \\\\ = [∑_(y)y^{2}f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid x)] - μ_{Y\\end{vmatrix}x}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find $f_{Y \\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x)$, let's first find the marginal distribution for $X$, corresponding to the row totals:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ | $f_X(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{5}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{3}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{5}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\nf_{Y \\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x) = \\dfrac{f(x,y)}{f_X(x)}\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x{:}$\n\n| $f_{Y \\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |  |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = 1\\end{bmatrix} &= [∑_(y)y^{2}f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid 1)] - μ_{Y \\mid 1}^{2} \\\\\n&= [1^{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} + 2^{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} + 3^{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}] - (\\frac{9}{4})^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4} + 1 + \\frac{9}{2} - \\frac{81}{16} \\\\\n&= \\frac{11}{16}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188327 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c80ef8f-1073-5e41-bec3-860209a731bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional Mass Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8efe7779-a68e-5320-9296-47bd49330142" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.69" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186091} {:answer/id #uuid "b9f78844-51fc-53d4-8e04-b0c325e2012f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186092} {:answer/id #uuid "0a1760c4-2536-5c77-a1ab-0e41464ef0b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186093} {:answer/id #uuid "0b97bdb2-55bb-51a0-a1e5-c0f1c24cfb35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186094} {:answer/id #uuid "53d94e20-9ee4-5882-97b4-bfc5c3196345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186095}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a8b5e94e-afe5-5762-95d7-8bafbffc617d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218